# English pyramid sweepstake

Parallel game to the World Cup sweepstake. Data lives in `app/data/english-pyramid-fantasy.ts`.

## Structure

- Seven managers, **fourteen clubs each** — one **title** pick and one **survival** pick from each division at draft (Premier League → National League South). Clubs that promote/relegate keep scoring in their new division via `divisionId` (e.g. York City drafted as NL, now League Two for 2026/27) but retain `draftDivisionId` for fairness ranks and squad badges.
- **Title draft:** pre-season outright winner betting odds within each **draft** division (lower decimal = stronger favourite). Each manager gets **exactly one pick at each odds rank** (1st favourite through 7th) spread across the seven divisions — player index `p` takes rank `((p + divisionIndex) mod 7) + 1`.
- **Survival draft:** bottom 7 by relegation odds (or longest title shots where markets are thin). **Same ordinal** within each league as the title pick: title rank `k` pairs with survival rank `k` (R#1 = relegation favourite / “20th favourite”) — `p` takes survival rank `((p + divisionIndex) mod 7) + 1`. So Arsenal #1 comes with Hull R#1; across seven rungs everyone still gets each rank once per band.
- Scoring (`ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_SCORING`): **3** home win, **4** away win, **1** draw (any score except 0–0), **−1** for a boring 0–0 (overrides draw + clean-sheet), **+1** clean sheet, **+1** for 3+ goals scored, **−1** for 3+ conceded, **+1** per red card.
- **League season only — no knockouts, no cups, no elimination.** All fourteen clubs score points all season. Do not apply World Cup bracket, knockout survival, or “teams left” logic to this game.

- **Prize pot:** `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_PRIZE_FUND` in `app/data/english-pyramid-fantasy.ts` tracks the cash pot invested in an all-world accumulating fund (default Yahoo symbol `VWRP.L`). Leave `units` / `purchasePriceGbp` / `investedAt` null until invested; then fill those three fields and the API will value the pot live (cached ~1h). UI panel sits above overall standings.

## 7 August re-draft (when asked)

When the user asks to redraw squads to current betting odds (planned ~7 Aug 2026):

- **Do not ask the user for odds sources.** Research them the same way as the original draft: web search UK bookmaker / odds-roundup pages (Goal.com, BettingLounge, BetVictor, Sky Bet, Bet365, Betfair, Racing Post, Football League World, News & Star, etc.). Note the source on each club’s `oddsNote`. Where NL North/South markets are thin, estimate ranks from published favourites / season previews and say so in `oddsNote`.
- **Do not ask the user to confirm which division each club is in.** By re-draft day, published outright / relegation markets list clubs in their **2026/27** divisions — trust those markets for `divisionId` / draft pools.
- Keep the same fairness formula and title↔survival pairing (`((p + divisionIndex + DRAFT_SEAT_OFFSET) mod 7) + 1`). `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_DRAFT_SEAT_OFFSET` (currently 3) rotates seats so a redraw does not inherit the previous PL #1 holder. Rebuild the title top-7 + survival bottom-7 per division, reassign `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_PLAYERS`, refresh fixtures if the club set changes, push `origin/main` unless asked otherwise.
### Reveal night (7pm Friday)

- `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_REDRAW` in `app/data/english-pyramid-fantasy.ts` holds `revealAtUtc` (**7pm Europe/London = 18:00 UTC in BST**), `headline`, and `hideSquadsUntilReveal`.
- A countdown banner sits at the top of `/p/ep2627` until `revealAtUtc`, then flips to “Play the reveal”. If the page is open when the clock strikes, the ceremony auto-launches once (guarded by localStorage).
- **When pushing the redrafted squads before 7pm, set `hideSquadsUntilReveal: true`.** The API then blanks `teams`, `teamBreakdown`, `draftNote`, fixture schedule, and club counts until the reveal time, so the new draw cannot be read early. It unlocks automatically on the clock — no second deploy needed (flip the flag back to `false` at leisure).
- Until Friday 7pm the public UI should look undrawn (sealed squad cards, “Sealed” in standings, no fixtures). The real squad data can already be in the repo behind that gate.
- Recordable ceremony opens from the banner button after 7pm, or any time until `ceremonyEndsAtUtc` via `/p/ep2627?reveal=1` (rehearsal path — there is deliberately no header button; API soft-unlocks `revealPlayers` with `?rehearsal=1` while public standings stay sealed). Full-screen, no scrolling, slot-machine shuffle that settles each of the 14 clubs per manager. Space/→ next · ← back · **P** pause · Esc exit.
- `ceremonyEndsAtUtc` (default: one hour before the first league KO) retires the countdown banner, “Play the reveal” button, and `?reveal=1` path. Squads stay unlocked; the page is just the normal game from then on.

## Shared UI

- `EnglishPyramidFantasy.tsx` wraps `WorldCupFantasy.tsx` with pyramid data, scoring helpers, and copy. UI improvements (W/L/D on results, bonus/penalty labels on team lines, manager photo cache busting, lightbox, etc.) belong in `WorldCupFantasy.tsx` and apply to **both** sweepstakes automatically.
- Per-game scoring display uses `getTeamMatchDisplay()` from `app/lib/english-pyramid-scoring.ts` (clean sheet bonus included).

## Fixtures and kick-off times

- Maintain `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FIXTURES` with **every league match** involving our **98 clubs** (not just games between sweepstake clubs).
- Refresh the bulk schedule with `npm run english-pyramid:fetch-fixtures -- --write` (ESPN: PL → NL; Football Web Pages: NL North/South).
- **National League (tier 5)** fixtures typically publish around **10 July** each summer. `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-fixture-check.yml` polls ESPN twice daily **10–20 July** (plus weekly Mondays) and auto-commits when eng.5 fixtures appear.
- **NL North / South** come from Football Web Pages team fixture pages (`scripts/lib/english-pyramid-fwp-nln-nls.cjs`). Same fetch/check commands refresh them; kick-offs are Europe/London → UTC. If FWP returns Cloudflare 403, the fetcher falls back to BBC Sport month fixture pages.
- **League only** — cup ties (FA Cup, League Cup, etc.) are excluded automatically (season slug + single-leg pair filter; FWP filters to `national-league-north` / `national-league-south` only).
- Weekly GitHub Action `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-fixture-check.yml` compares remote sources to the repo and auto-refreshes when kick-offs move (international breaks, postponements).
- Manual drift check: `npm run english-pyramid:check-fixtures` (add `--write` to apply).
- First matchday opens on the earliest fixture date in the ledger (e.g. Championship often kicks off Friday before the main Saturday batch).
- Store `utcDate` as **UTC ISO-8601** (`2026-08-09T14:00:00Z`) converted from the **Europe/London** kick-off (handles GMT/BST).
- Typical UK kick-offs: **12:30**, **15:00**, **17:30** (weekend), **19:45** / **20:00** (midweek). Full-time is usually ~115 minutes later.
- Fixture ids: stable keys such as `2026-08-09-ars-che` (date + home code + away code).
- When recording a result, roll fixtures forward — add the next known upcoming sweepstake fixture(s) so the UI keeps showing what is next.

## Manual / agent score updates

When asked to update English pyramid scores (or by the scheduled GitHub workflow):

- Append finished **league** matches to `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_MANUAL_MATCHES` only — one ledger for all seven divisions.
- Only look for **newly finished** games not already in the manual ledger. Do not re-verify recorded entries.
- Use team codes from `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_TEAM_BY_CODE` / `getEnglishPyramidTeamSearchTerms()` (club name variants for matching).
- Check reliable UK sources: BBC Sport, Sky Sports, official league/club sites, Flashscore.
- Add only final results: home/away teams (`tla` code), final goals, red-card tallies (including second-yellow dismissals).
- Cross-check red-card tallies against ESPN before finishing any score update: run `npm run english-pyramid:validate` (includes `scripts/english-pyramid-validate-red-cards.cjs`). If ESPN reports reds for a finished ledger match and the ledger is lower, fix the ledger before pushing.
- When appending a new manual result, always set explicit `homeRedCards` and `awayRedCards` (use `0` when none). Never omit the fields.
- FWP-synced NL North/South results set `redsUnchecked: true` (reds default to 0). When you verify a dismissal from BBC/Flashscore/Sky, set the correct red tallies and remove `redsUnchecked`.
- **Every manual result must exist in `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FIXTURES` with matching home/away TLAs.** The full-season fixture list is kept in-repo (unlike the rolling World Cup schedule), so `npm run english-pyramid:validate` fails if the ledger and fixtures drift apart or if a fixture is overdue with no result.
- Do not hand-edit standings — `computeStandings()` in `app/lib/english-pyramid-scoring.ts` derives totals.
- After any ledger change, run `npm run english-pyramid:standings` and use that output as the only source for totals and leader/bottom wording in `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_FANTASY_DAILY_UPDATE`.
- Automated sync refreshes a **named recap** roast via `npm run english-pyramid:roast -- --write` when new results land (`english-pyramid-ci-sync-commit`). It must name managers and clubs, include every current total, and never dump TLA scorelines (`WBA 3-1 BUR`) or the old three-line insult templates. `npm run english-pyramid:validate` fails those. Prefer a sharper agent/manual roast when you can; still mirror standings totals exactly and do not invent scores. Tone: **fouler Grok / Tesla cabin energy** - sweary, rude, British football roast, genuinely funny. Name managers and clubs. Short paragraphs separated by blank lines. **Never use em dashes or en dashes** (scores are `0-1`, not `0–1`). Avoid repeating the same gag.
- Push to **`origin/main`** unless the user asks for PR-only work.

## Scheduled workflow

- **Scores:** `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-score-agent.yml` runs `npm run english-pyramid:sync` for due fixtures on ESPN tiers (PL → NL) and **Football Web Pages for NL North/South**. Matchday sweeps may still need the Cursor agent for roast copy / edge cases.
- **NL North / South results:** same sync job scrapes FWP team fixture pages (kick-off cells become `1 - 0` when final). Red cards are recorded as `0` with `redsUnchecked: true` (FWP tables do not expose dismissals reliably). UI labels those results “(reds unchecked)”; cross-check Flashscore/BBC and clear the flag when verified.
- **Auto roast:** after a successful ledger sync that appends matches, CI runs `english-pyramid-refresh-roast.cjs` so the Daily roast is a named recap of that day (managers, clubs, fantasy points, full table). Agent can overwrite with funnier copy. Validation rejects TLA dumps and the old filler templates.
- **Live UI scores:** ESPN for PL→NL; Football Web Pages competition day pages for NLN/NLS (`app/lib/english-pyramid-fwp-live-scores.ts`), polled with the matchday API refresh.
- **Due fixtures:** `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` keeps fixtures due until recorded (no lookback expiry), with a matchday sweep fallback for same-day games.
- **Due fixtures:** `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` keeps fixtures due until recorded (no lookback expiry), with a matchday sweep fallback for same-day games.
- **Health check:** `.github/workflows/english-pyramid-health-check.yml` runs `npm run english-pyramid:validate` on a fixed schedule and fails loudly on overdue fixtures or ESPN red-card drift.
- **Validate split:** `npm run english-pyramid:validate:scores` (ledger + reds + roast), `npm run english-pyramid:validate` (same).

`.github/workflows/english-pyramid-score-agent.yml` runs on UK matchday windows (Europe/London), not US World Cup hours:

- **Weekends**: frequent checks ~14:10–22:50 London for 12:30 / 15:00 / 17:30 / evening KO batches.
- **Midweek**: checks ~21:00–22:50 London for 19:45 / 20:00 KOs.
- `scripts/english-pyramid-due-fixtures.cjs` decides when to trigger based on fixture kick-offs + 115 minute delay, with a matchday sweep fallback.

## Example Slack / agent prompt

> Sync English pyramid sweepstake scores. Find newly finished matches for our 98 clubs across PL → NL South, append to `ENGLISH_PYRAMID_MANUAL_MATCHES`, refresh fixtures and daily roast, merge to main, push origin/main.
